"A very short unified proof of Dar&#39;s conjecture and Log-Brunn--Minkowski in the plane | ArcXiv (https://arcxiv.org/abs/2609.08495)\nciteturn3search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 4 weeks ago; # A very short unified proof of Dar's conjecture and Log-Brunn--Minkowski in the plane ... This short note gives a very short unified proof of both Dar's conjecture and the log-Brunn--Minkowski inequality in the plane.\n\n# A very short unified proof of Dar's conjecture and Log-Brunn--Minkowski in the plane\n\nDongmeng Xi\n\nSeptember 8, 2026·math.MG·arXiv:2609.08495\n\n## Abstract\n\nThis short note gives a very short unified proof of both Dar's conjecture and the log-Brunn--Minkowski inequality in the plane. A planar Lp-Brunn-Minkowski inequality for p∈ [-∞,0] is established and gives the two key inequalities at p=0 and p=-∞. Motivated by this new proof, the author proposes a related conjecture in 3, to attack the two conjectures in higher dimensions.\n\n\nOpen PDF Open on arXiv Share\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA note on the quantitative local version of the log-Brunn-Minkowski inequality (https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.10708)\nciteturn3academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.0 years ago; Title: A note on the quantitative local version of the log-Brunn-Minkowski inequality\nTitle: A note on the quantitative local version of the log-Brunn-Minkowski inequality\nAuthors: Andrea Colesanti, Galyna V. Livshyts\nDate: Sun Oct 29 22:36:04 2017\n\nWe prove that the log-Brunn-Minkowski inequality \\begin{equation*} |\\lambda K+_0 (1-\\lambda)L|\\geq |K|^{\\lambda}|L|^{1-\\lambda} \\end{equation*} (where $|\\cdot|$ is the Lebesgue measure and $+_0$ is the so-called log-addition) holds when $K\\subset\\mathbb{R}^n$ is a ball and $L$ is a symmetric convex body in a suitable $C^2$ neighborhood of $K$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRichard M. Aron, Eva A. Gallardo